@{
    ViewBag.Title = "How Exchanges Work";
}

<main class="container my-5" style="max-width: 900px;">
    <h1 class="h2 mb-3">How an exchange works</h1>
    <p class="lead">SkillBridge helps two members teach each other, one skill in each direction.</p>

    <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered mb-4">
        <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Set up your profile.</strong> Choose a skill you can teach, a skill you want to learn, and the stage you know.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Find a reciprocal match.</strong> For example, Amina can teach Python and wants SQL. Rahim can teach SQL and wants Python.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Send a proposal.</strong> Amina asks to learn SQL and shares a goal, preferred pace, and first meeting idea. Rahim reviews it and chooses the skill he wants to learn from Amina.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Learn together.</strong> Each skill has up to seven stages. Both members confirm a stage when they agree it is complete.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Finish and rate.</strong> Once all stages in the exchange are confirmed, either member can complete the exchange. Both can then rate their experience.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-muted">You can read skills and community discussions before signing up. Requests, messages, and exchanges require an account.</p>
    <p class="text-muted">If an exchange cannot continue, either member can end it early and give a reason. It will not count as completed.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="@Url.Action("Skills", "Explore")">Browse skills</a>
    @if (!User.Identity.IsAuthenticated)
    {
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary ms-2" href="@Url.Action("Register", "Account")">Create an account</a>
    }
</main>
